From cf57de0d7d82a4b9b628ebed2a01e1bf331f9975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:34:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: release a dead local claim left on a
 non-running card; card read names it, self-heal agent-dc4177df2e

A status-only write (the sync feed's Board lease-expiry row) moved T6 t_01a1a09e94bfaa25 from running to ready
and left the dead worker's claim_lock/worker_pid: claim columns are local and never overwritten by a pull. The
dispatcher claims only claim_lock IS NULL cards and release_stale_claims/reconcile_orphaned_running look at
running only, so the card never started for 5 days and its read showed nothing.

- release_leftover_local_claims: every tick (not gated on a running card), clear this host's claim fields on
  ready/todo/review/blocked/scheduled/done cards whose worker is dead or gone; skips live pids, claims in flight
  and cards leased elsewhere; exact-value CAS; status unchanged; claim_released event reason=leftover_local_claim.
- kanban_queue_position: a ready card holding a claim_lock reads lane=leftover_claim with a queue_note, instead of
  a local-slot wait.
---
